From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:14:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: shell-drawn dialogs and downloads

Plan C12 (shell-drawn dialogs: JavaScript alert/confirm/prompt,
permission prompts, HTTP auth, file chooser, external protocol,
downloads; acceptance: each dialog has a SwiftUI view, behavior from
Chromium). Until now only JavaScript dialogs reached the shell; the rest
got default answers (permissions dismissed, no HTTP-auth prompt, no file
chooser, external apps never launched, downloads cancelled because
OACProfile.downloads was a stub).

//chrome's controllers still decide when to ask and what to remember;
the bridge replaces only their Views UI with OACDialogDelegate requests:

- Permissions: PermissionRequestManager's prompt view is the bridge's
  (openarc::DialogHost, registered at engine start). One
  OACPermissionRequest per prompt group (camera + microphone together);
  allow / allow this time / deny / dismiss map to Accept, AcceptThisTime,
  Deny and Dismiss, so Chrome stores decisions, one-time grants and its
  embargo as usual. supportsAllowingOnce follows Chrome's own rule
  (PermissionUtil::DoesSupportTemporaryGrants). getUserMedia reaches the
  manager through MediaCaptureDevicesDispatcher (the tab's
  WebContentsDelegate). The view withdraws its request when the manager
  destroys it (navigation, tab closed).
- HTTP auth: ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateHttpAuthCoordinator is
  overridden so Chrome's flow (extensions, LoginTabHelper for main-frame
  401/407 with its blank page and reload, password manager hookup) uses
  a LoginHandler whose view is an OACAuthenticationRequest.
- File chooser: the tab's WebContentsDelegate::RunFileChooser makes an
  OACFileChooserRequest (accept types as UTIs; folder upload enumerated
  by Chrome's FileSelectHelper).
- External protocol: ExternalProtocolHandler's embedder dialog hook (the
  previous patch) makes an OACExternalProtocolRequest; "Open" sets the
  block state when remembered and launches through Chrome. The tab gets
  Chrome's ExternalProtocolObserver so a user gesture permits the next
  launch, as a Browser tab's features do.
- Downloads: OACProfile.downloads is the profile's DownloadManager with
  //chrome's ChromeDownloadManagerDelegate (history, target paths,
  dangerous-file checks); items, observers with coalesced progress,
  pause / resume / cancel / keep or discard / remove, download location
  and "ask where to save". SAVE_TO_DISK opens become downloads.

Not done here: client certificate selection (continues without a
certificate, as before).
